    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d1148">

                <pb facs="1261" n="1251" xml:id="pg1251"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">711.71114A/9–2144: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to the
                        Ambassador in the Soviet Union</hi> (<hi
                            rendition="#italic">Harriman</hi>)<anchor n="64"
                        xml:id="d1148-f1"/>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1944-09-21T18:00:00-04:00">September 21,
                            1944—6 p.m.</date>
                    </dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>2255. Please express to the Soviet Government the appreciation of the Government
                    of the United States for the assistance rendered by Soviet military authorities
                    in arranging for the evacuation of American prisoners of war held by the enemy
                    in the Balkan countries. Special assistance was given in the evacuation of
                    American airmen from the vicinity of Ploesti by General Burenin who was most
                    cooperative.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Hull</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d1148-f1" n="64" type="source" xml:id="d1148-f1-content">
                <p>This telegram was in response to a request from the Office of Strategic Services
                    forwarded to the Department by Mr. Kirk in telegram No. 339, September 9, 1944,
                    from Caserta. Officials of the Office of Strategic Services in Bucharest had
                    asked that a message of appreciation be sent to the Soviet Government for
                    assistance rendered by the Red Army in evacuating American prisoners from the
                    Ploesti region. (711.71114A/9–944)</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
